# Upload trimming for the ARQ worker service ONLY.
#
# The worker is the one service deployed from the REPO ROOT (see railway.toml for why its
# config file cannot live in backend/). Without this file every `railway up` from the root
# would upload frontend assets/reports, the landing site, docs and load tests. The worker
# needs frontend compiler/kernel inputs, but does not copy those unrelated artifacts.
#
# This file is never consulted by the API or frontend deploys: those run
# `cd backend|frontend && railway up . --path-as-root`, so the repo root is not their
# archive root and this file is not in their upload.
#
# `railway up` already honors .gitignore, so node_modules/.venv/build output need no entry.

# The worker compiles the same nesting kernel as the browser. Keep its package
# lock, source and profile-verified build tools in the archive; omit unrelated output.
frontend/build/
frontend/dist/
frontend/public/
frontend/e2e/
frontend/coverage/
frontend/playwright-report/
frontend/test-results/
frontend/.browser-harness/
frontend/tools/browser-harness/
backend/nesting-runtime/
landing/
load-tests/
docs/
nginx/
supabase/
signature/
e2e/
.github/
.claude/
